    "body": "@beaufortfrancois I was thinking the same (But didn't get time today to try). Will try it tomorrow.\r\n_Persistence sounds better over chance_  in theory. \r\nSo we can do a `try catch` _DOM Exception ..._ (i.e try to catch the failure info I was getting earlier as a result of it being unable to open the port (for potential reasons as mentioned by @reillyeon)) and then try again till it succeeds.    \r\n\r\nSomething like this may be 🤔 :\r\n```js\r\nwhile (true){\r\n    try {\r\n        await port.open({ baudRate: baudrate});\r\n        if (port) break;\r\n    } catch(err){\r\n        // log ...\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```",
