    "created_at": "2026-10-01T21:54:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T21:54:47Z",
    "body": "This reinforces why #128 is the prerequisite.\n\nA reconnect algorithm should not need to repeatedly call `open()` until one succeeds. With a stable origin-scoped port ID, the application could retain the intended logical port, observe a matching `connect` event, and attempt exactly one reopen.\n\nThat would remove both ambiguity and the high-frequency retry loop shown earlier in this thread.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
